      <VERS vnumber="9">And <gr str="3258">Jabez </gr>was more <gr str="3513">honourable </gr>than his <gr str="251">brethren</gr>: and his <gr str="517">mother </gr>
        <gr str="7121">called </gr>his <gr str="8034">name </gr>
        <gr str="3258">Jabez</gr>, <gr str="559">saying</gr>, Because I <gr str="3205">bore </gr>him with <gr str="6090">sorrow</gr>. <DIV>
          <NOTE type="x-studynote">Jabez: that is, Sorrowful</NOTE>
        </DIV>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="10">And <gr str="3258">Jabez </gr>
        <gr str="7121">called </gr>on the <gr str="430">God </gr>of <gr str="3478">Israel</gr>, <gr str="559">saying</gr>, O <gr str="518">that </gr>thou wouldest <gr str="1288">bless </gr>me <gr str="1288">indeed</gr>, and <gr str="7235">enlarge </gr>my <gr str="1366">land</gr>, and that thy <gr str="3027">hand </gr>might be with me, and that thou wouldest <gr str="6213">keep </gr>
        <STYLE css="font-style:italic">me</STYLE> from <gr str="7451">evil</gr>, that it may not <gr str="6087">grieve </gr>me! And <gr str="430">God </gr>
        <gr str="935">granted </gr>him that which he <gr str="7592">requested</gr>. <DIV>
          <NOTE type="x-studynote">Oh…: Heb. If thou wilt, etc</NOTE>
        </DIV>
        <DIV>
          <NOTE type="x-studynote">keep…: Heb. do me</NOTE>
        </DIV>
      </VERS>
